TOPIC:
Limitations and Theoretical Context

EXAMPLES:
['Six-bit string symmetry: A network with only two hidden units can identify '
 'symmetric strings by learning symmetric input-to-hidden weights that result '
 'in zero net input for symmetric patterns.']

INTUITION:
['Think of hidden units as little detectives that the network trains itself. '
 'If you want to detect symmetry, the network learns to have one part of the '
 'unit look for the left side and another part look for the right side; when '
 "they match, they cancel each other out to say 'this is symmetric'."]

REASONING:
['Hidden layers are powerful because they allow the network to construct '
 'useful internal representations that make complex mappings learnable.',
 'Increasing the dimensionality of the weight space can help the optimization '
 'process bypass barriers caused by non-convex loss surfaces.']

WHY IT MATTERS:
['It proves that networks can learn useful internal features automatically, '
 'removing the need for humans to manually design features for every specific '
 'problem.']
