['Context window: A sequence of 4 tokens is fed into the network. Given the '
 'vocabulary size of 100,277, the network outputs 100,277 probabilities. If '
 "the next token is 'post' (ID 3962), the model adjusts its internal weights "
 'to increase the 3% probability assigned to that token.']

INTUITION:
['Think of the neural network parameters like knobs on a DJ set; as you '
 "'twiddle' the knobs, you change how the network processes inputs. Training "
 "is the process of finding the right knob settings so the machine 'learns' "
 'the patterns in the data.',
 "Inference is like flipping a biased coin where the 'bias' is determined by "
 "the neural network's confidence; tokens the model thinks are more likely "
 'have a higher chance of being picked.']

REASONING:
["The neural network's parameters are adjusted because random initialization "
 'produces random predictions; iterative updates ensure the model internalizes '
 'the statistics of how tokens follow each other in the training data.',
 'Sampling from the probability distribution is used during inference because '
 'it allows the model to generate remixes of data that are statistically '
 'similar to the training set but not necessarily verbatim reproductions.']

WHY IT MATTERS:
['Understanding training vs. inference clarifies that when using tools like '
 "ChatGPT, the model is not 'learning' from your input in real-time; the "
 'parameters are fixed, and it is purely performing inference.']
