Future Trends in LLM Development

EXAMPLES:
['Comparison of decimals: A model may struggle to identify that 9.9 is larger '
 'than 9.11, despite its ability to solve advanced Olympiad-level mathematics '
 'problems.']

INTUITION:
['Treat LLMs like a tool or a draft-maker rather than an infallible expert; '
 "they have 'holes in the Swiss cheese' where they can solve complex Olympiad "
 'math but fail on simple logical tasks like comparing decimals (9.11 vs 9.9).',
 "Multimodality isn't a fundamental change in logic, just a change in input "
 'format: once you turn audio and images into tokens, the model treats them '
 'exactly the same way it treats text.']

REASONING:
['Scaling context windows alone will not suffice for long-running multimodal '
 'tasks, necessitating research into new architectures beyond simple context '
 'length expansion.',
 'Human-to-agent ratios are predicted to become necessary in digital '
 'workflows, mirroring human-to-robot ratios in factory automation for '
 'supervising model actions.']

WHY IT MATTERS:
['Awareness of model fallibility prevents over-reliance; users must remain '
 'responsible for the final output.',
 'Understanding future directions like agents and multimodal integration helps '
 'practitioners prepare for shifts in how models are supervised and deployed.']
